{
  "_comment": [
    "Measurement keys: the vocabulary that lets a glued word such as 'hb13.5'",
    "or 'pco2:45' be split into a key and a value.",
    "",
    "A key is used for splitting only when it either consumes the whole word or",
    "is followed by a digit. That restriction is what stops the route alias",
    "'in' from splitting 'insulin' into 'in' + 'sulin'.",
    "",
    "Keys that contain digits are the ones that genuinely need to be here:",
    "'pco2' and 'hb13' are lexically identical, so no rule distinguishes them",
    "and only a lexicon can. Digit-free keys such as 'hb' are listed for their",
    "display names and dimensions; splitting would find them anyway.",
    "",
    "Adding an analyte is a data change. This file is user-overridable through",
    "the same .config mechanism as every other lexicon file, so a clinic can",
    "add local assay names without touching the engine.",
    "",
    "'dimension' names a group in units.json and is advisory: it drives display",
    "and unit recognition. ClinLang does not check whether a value is plausible.",
    "No reference ranges are defined here or anywhere else in the engine."
  ],

  "measurements": {
